WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.402 line:7%
 My name is Josh Weston.

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:05.538 line:0%
I got into bladesmithing
from Spartacus.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:12.912 line:0%
Something inside me lit on
fire, and I had to make swords.

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:14.547 line:7%
 I'm Jason Redick.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.817 line:0%
I started making blades when I
was a kid with my grandfather.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.253
I'm 100% self-taught.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.422
[soft music]

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.158
 Jason.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.359
Josh.

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.795
Congratulations, you've
made it to the final round.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.396
When you came here
we asked you to forge

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:34.500
a blade in your signature style
using our tools and our forges.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.168
Now we're sending
you home to create

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:37.837
an iconic blade from history--

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.173
[dramatic music]

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:43.976
--the kukri.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:44.710
 Hell, yes.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:45.944
[dramatic music]

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.547
WIL WILLIS
(VOICEOVER): The kukri

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.382
is a blade issued to Nepalese
soldiers, known as the Gurkhas.

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:53.486
During the Anglo-Nepalese war
in the early 19th century,

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.623
the kukri became renowned
in the Western world for its

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.657
versatility on the battlefield.

00:00:58.724 --> 00:01:02.328
The kukri's unique curved
design, and angle of the blade,

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:06.566
gives it the ability to slice
and chop simultaneously.

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:10.002
The Gurkha soldiers were said
to be so skilled with kukri

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.939
that it acted as an
extension of their arm.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:16.275
Today, the kukri is far
more visible worldwide,

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.312
seen in films like "Resident
Evil Extinction," and

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.214
"Big Trouble in Little China."

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:27.653
 It must be a fully
functioning, authentic version

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.288
of that deadly weapon.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:33.259 line:0%
 I'm really nervous
because I know literally

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:36.429 line:7%
nothing about this blade.

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.532
 You will have five days
to complete this challenge.

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.866
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:44.036
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.539 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.442
 Let's crank the heat.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.377
[blade sharpening]

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:56.048
 Whoa!

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:58.785
 I am very, very happy.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.052
Me likey.

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.454
JOSH WESTON: The mid-bar
is welded together.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:04.957
I've drawn out a
new piece of steel.

00:02:05.023 --> 00:02:07.393
I'm forge welding them together.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:10.462
There's a lot of
forging left to be done.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:13.399
I am doing my damnedest
to win this thing.

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:16.269
I've got to try to
punch this thing.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:19.872
It's going to be difficult
to get an even temperature.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.207
JOSH WESTON (VOICEOVER): The
quench is the most critical

00:02:22.274 --> 00:02:25.778
part of the sword build.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:26.545
 All right.

00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:27.547
Who's ready?

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.815
JOSH WESTON: This is it.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:31.517
If this blade doesn't
survive the quench, I'm sunk.

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.753
There's just no
coming back from it.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:39.225
 Three, two, one.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.166
JOSH WESTON: I'm
finding absolutely

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.101
nothing wrong with this blade.

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:52.571
Everything is exactly
as it should be.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.240
I have a blade!

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.709 line:7%
Whoa, ha, whoa!

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.312 line:7%
[music playing]

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.316
JASON REDICK: Now that I'm back
home, I feel much more at ease.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.250
I'm used to my equipment.

00:03:05.317 --> 00:03:06.952
I've got a wonderful family.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:09.923
And if I could
win this, it would

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:11.857
mean all the support
that my family has

00:03:11.924 --> 00:03:13.492
given me over the years is--

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.229
you know, they've
been correct to do it.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:20.633 line:0%
This is a lot larger of a
kukri than I've made before.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.402 line:0%
So it's going to be a little
bit more forging and stuff

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.870 line:7%
than what I'm used to.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.105 line:7%
Yeah.

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:27.373 line:0%
I wish the head was
a little bit wider.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.241 line:7%
I think it'll be all right.

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:31.410
Got the blade shaped
up the way I wanted.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.846
The blade seems
nice and straight.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.282
I'm leaving it to cool now.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.150
We're good, and I
can heat treat it.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.621
[music playing]

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:46.192
Got to be real careful
not to move it.

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.861
Just let this thing sit
still inside the oil,

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:52.632
and completely cool down.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:57.903
At this point I hope I got
time to get everything done.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:01.441
[sharpening]

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:08.180
JASON REDICK: All right.

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:11.718
[upbeat music]

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:16.622
JOSH WESTON: That's good.

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:19.492
[slow music]

00:04:20.392 --> 00:04:22.594
 Jason, Josh, welcome back.

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:24.730
Many battles Gurkha
soldiers have fought

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.299
were defending forts,
just like this one.

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:29.268
So we thought it would
be an ideal place

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:30.469
to test your kukris.

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.304
We will now put
both of your weapons

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:33.906
through a series of tests.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:36.108
First up, the strength test.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.610
Doug.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:40.446
DOUG: Bladesmiths, Kukris
were multipurpose knives

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:41.981
as well as weapons of war.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:45.217
It was also used commonly to
clear the fields of Nepal,

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:46.986
as well as chop wood.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.022
To test the strength
of your kukri,

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:52.325
I will cut through
these sugar canes.

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.092
Jason, you're up.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:53.825
You ready?

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:55.395
 I'm ready.

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:58.264 line:0%
I'm getting nervous, because
it's all out of my hands now.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:01.768
[upbeat music]

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:13.012
 Well, Jason.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:14.980
This is a beast.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:16.449
 Thank you.

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.951
 I do not see any indentations
in your blade, at all.

00:05:19.017 --> 00:05:20.619
So it cut nicely.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.922
But the handle construction
is very hard to hold

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:25.124
onto because it's very smooth.

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.325
 Yeah.

00:05:26.391 --> 00:05:29.262
DOUG: But, once
again, it did its job.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:29.962
Good job.

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:30.830
 Thank you.

00:05:30.896 --> 00:05:31.997
 Josh, you're up.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:32.965
You're ready?

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:34.567
 I'm ready.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.836 line:0%
Is this thing even going
to hold up and come

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.304 line:7%
out in one piece at the end?

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:39.271 line:7%
I have no idea.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.809
[upbeat music]

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.419
 Well, Josh, I don't
see any indentations

00:05:54.486 --> 00:05:56.422
on your edge over here.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.823
I like the balance.

00:05:57.923 --> 00:06:00.493
Your handle is nice and
comfortable around the hand.

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.495
I was able to maintain
control of it.

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:07.132
And the edge is sharp enough to
cut through these sugar canes.

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:08.700
Good job.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:10.970
JOSH WESTON: I think coming
out of the sugar cane test--

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.705
we're at a tie right now.

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:17.276
 All right, gentlemen,
next up is the kill test.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.511
The kukri is a powerful
weapon in combat--

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:22.981
so much so that in 1814,
22,000 British soldiers

00:06:23.048 --> 00:06:26.318
went up against 600 Gurkhas,
armed with the kukri.

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:28.054
The British suffered
massive losses

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.323
and the Gurkhas
never surrendered.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:34.260
Thus began the legend and
reputation of the kukri.

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:36.963
To test of lethality and
function of your blade,

00:06:37.063 --> 00:06:38.364
I will take your
kukri and I will

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.331
slash through these carcasses.

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.134
[dramatic beats]

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:42.801
DOUG: Jason, you're up.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:43.302
 All right.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.404
Let's go.

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:47.006
My heart's beating.

00:06:47.072 --> 00:06:50.776
Any time you cut bone, it's
very, very hard on the blade.

00:06:50.842 --> 00:06:53.112
If you're going to get a chip
or something in your blade,

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:55.213
it's going to happen when
you cut through bone.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:59.419
[dramatic music]

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:14.866
 Well, Jason, the beast
over here, it cuts.

00:07:14.933 --> 00:07:16.735
Just the way it sliced
through this time,

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:19.238
I felt the nice
curve in your design.

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:22.341
This, sir, will kill.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:23.776
 Thank you.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:24.343
 Josh, you're up.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:25.110
You ready?

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.378
 Let's do it.

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:29.014
I'm half excited and
half [bleep] my pants.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:33.986
[dramtic music]

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:45.031
 Well, Josh, your blade didn't
slash all the way through

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.232
the carcasses, but it did cut.

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:51.070
And those kinds
of cuts will kill.

00:07:54.039 --> 00:07:57.509
WIL WILLIS: Jason, Josh,
you were given five

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.745
days at your home
forge to design

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:02.448
and fabricate signature kukris.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:04.683
You've both done
a fantastic job.

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:07.586
This was a very
difficult decision,

00:08:07.686 --> 00:08:10.322
but there can only be one
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:13.658
[dramatic sound effect]

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:18.998
WIL WILLIS: Jason,
congratulations.

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:22.701
Josh, unfortunately, you
did not make the cut.

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:25.004
 Josh, when I saw your
blade in the strength test,

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:28.307
the way it performed, I
expected it to continue

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:29.575
performing that way.

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:31.610
And your edge retention
didn't hold up.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.779
So that's why I
have to let you go.

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:36.848
WIL WILLIS: Josh, please
surrender your weapon.

00:08:36.915 --> 00:08:39.618
 I am disappointed,
but what I've

00:08:39.718 --> 00:08:43.155
learned from this
experience is invaluable.

00:08:43.255 --> 00:08:46.425
And even though I didn't walk
away with 10 grand today,

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:47.926
I don't feel like a loser.

00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:50.996
So that's a really nice
relief at the end of it.

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:53.532
 Jason, congratulations,
you are the "Forged in Fire"

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:57.235
champion, which comes
with a $10,000 check.

00:08:57.302 --> 00:08:58.604
 Yes.

00:08:58.671 --> 00:09:00.472
I just won 10 grand.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.840
Oh, god, am I--

00:09:01.907 --> 00:09:04.576
I'm so happy right
now I can barely talk.

00:09:04.676 --> 00:09:05.944
 Man, you got a beast there.

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:07.146
 [chuckles]

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:08.246
 That thing-- you get that
in motion, that's going

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:09.081
to keep going and going.

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:09.916
JASON REDICK: Oh, yeah.

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:10.816
 That edge great.

00:09:10.883 --> 00:09:11.783
 Thank you.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:14.253
I came here to
prove that I'm doing

00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:15.921
the right thing with my life.

00:09:15.987 --> 00:09:18.290
And I feel like I've
accomplished all that.

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:20.626
I'll be bragging about this
for a long time to come.

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:23.829
[dramatic music]

